# elements.md: required elements, sfvictorian-split

Coordinates are plan.md's (x 0..15 W→E, z 0 street/N → 49, y 0 = street). Part numbers: P1 shell, P2 front massing, P3 roofs & cornice, P4 openings & window dressing, P5 ornament, P6 site. Vocab names are defined in plan.md VOCABULARY. Colour roles: BODY cyan_terracotta, TRIM smooth_quartz, PLUM purple_terracotta / crimson_*, GOLD yellow_terracotta + orange_terracotta, STONE stone_bricks, IRON iron_bars.

- [ ] **1 Tall narrow three-storey front over a garage base**: body 16 wide, y0..17 (+bay y4..16). Garage plinth stone y0..3 under three painted storeys (y4..16), parapet y18. Real construction: stone_bricks plinth, `siding` walls on z=7 x0..9 / x15, bay walls y4..16. P1 (z=7 wall, party walls, slabs y0/4/9/13/17), P2 (plinth+bay). Vocab: `rusticated`, `siding`.
- [ ] **2 Garage door and drive**: opening x3..6 y1..3 z4. Plum panelled door: crimson_planks fill with `crimson_trapdoor` closed (half=bottom, facing south) as raised panels at (3,1..3)...(6,1..3) in a 2×3 pattern, framed by a cream lintel `smooth_quartz_slab` row at (3..6,4,3) and ledge. Drive apron light_gray_concrete x3..6 z0..3 y0. P4 (door), P6 (apron). Vocab: `garageDoor`.
- [ ] **3 Stair of steps up to the entry (stoop)**: stair blocks `stone_brick_stairs` facing south at (11..13,1,2),(11..13,2,3),(11..13,3,4),(11..13,4,5); landing stone_bricks (11..13,4,6); stone_bricks filling under each tread to y0; cheeks stone_bricks x10/x14 (y1..4 stepping with the treads); iron_bars handrail on each cheek top. P2. Vocab: `stoop`.
- [ ] **4 Recessed entry porch with columns**: floor y4 (stand y5) x10..14 z7..9 stone_bricks, ceiling y9 plum coffer (crimson_planks with `crimson_trapdoor` inset), void y5..8; two columns at (10,5..8,7),(14,5..8,7); BODY side walls x=9, x=15 with cream wainscot (`smooth_quartz_slab` bottom y5 rows). Front wall z=7 omitted x10..14 y5..8. P2 (floor, ceiling, walls), P5 (columns). Vocab: `column`, `porchWainscot`.
- [ ] **5 Columns**: base `smooth_quartz_slab` type=bottom at y5; shaft `quartz_pillar` axis=y at y6..7; capital `smooth_quartz_stairs` half=top facing=south (lip outward) at y8; at (10,·,7) and (14,·,7). P5. Vocab: `column`.
- [ ] **6 Entry door + transom**: back wall z=10 x11..12 y5..7: `crimson_door` (two doors side by side, hinges outward, facing north) with hung `glass_pane` transom at (11..12,8,10); casing smooth_quartz stairs/slabs both sides; lantern hanging in porch at (12,8,8) (`lantern` hanging=true). P4. Vocab: `entryDoor`.
- [ ] **7 Full-height angled bay stacked up the front**: rows z4 x3..6 face; diagonals (2,5),(7,5),(1,6),(8,6); y4..16; bay floors at y4 (plinth top), y9, y13 over x3..6 z5, x2..7 z6; lid y17 over the bay rows. Walls `siding`; spandrels at y9 (`spandrel`, purple_terracotta) and y13 (`fishscale`). Cream corner boards (`quartz_pillar` axis=y) replace the wall block at (3,4),(6,4),(2,5),(7,5),(1,6),(8,6) y4..16. P2. Vocab: `bayWall`, `cornerBoard`.
- [ ] **8 Tall narrow double-hung windows with ornate pediments and trim**: every window in plan.md OPENINGS; glass_pane fill, plum `crimson_trapdoor` open=true shutters-as-casing NOT used; casing = smooth_quartz_stairs/blocks; sill `smooth_quartz_slab` +1 at y4/9/13; pediment hood: pair = two `crimson_stairs` (facing east at left cell, west at right) + `smooth_quartz_slab` bottom caps at one cell above the head (y8,13,16); singles = `smooth_quartz_slab`. P4. Vocab: `window`, `hoodPair`, `hoodSingle`, `sill`.
- [ ] **9 Elaborate bracketed cornice**: y17 `smooth_quartz_stairs` half=top facing into wall at z=6 x0,9..15 and the bay ring (z=3 x2..7; (1,4),(8,4),(0,5),(9,5)); lid beneath; paired plum `crimson_stairs` half=top brackets at y16 below it; plum dentils `crimson_trapdoor` half=top closed at y16 between brackets. Returns 1 cell on the party walls at z=7..8 y16..17. P3 (cornice course), P5 (brackets, dentils). Vocab: `cornice`, `bracket`, `dentils`.
- [ ] **10 False-front parapet with centre pediment**: y18 z=7 x0..15 `siding` (BODY), coping `smooth_quartz_slab` bottom y19 at z=6..7 x1..5,10..14; pediment (6..9,19,7): x6 `smooth_quartz_stairs` facing east, x7..8 yellow_terracotta, x9 stairs facing west; crown `smooth_quartz_slab` at (7..8,20,7). Ball finials at (0,19,7),(15,19,7): `smooth_quartz` + `end_rod` above. P3. Vocab: `parapet`, `pediment`, `finial`.
- [ ] **11 Fish-scale shingles + horizontal siding**: siding is the wall block everywhere; fish scale: `fishscale` panel (yellow_terracotta/orange_terracotta staggered, 2 rows) on y13 spandrel of bay faces/diagonals, y16 frieze between brackets across z=7 x0..15 and bay faces z=4,diagonals, and in the pediment tympanum. P2 (y13 band), P5 (y16 frieze).
- [ ] **12 Painted-lady colours (≥3 body+trim)**: BODY teal cyan_terracotta, TRIM white smooth_quartz, PLUM purple_terracotta/crimson, GOLD yellow+orange terracotta, grey stone, black iron. All parts.
- [ ] **13 Tiny front garden behind an iron fence**: beds at plan SITE (soil `dirt`/`coarse_dirt` at y0, flowers y1: red_tulip, poppy, allium, azure_bluet, lilac, flowering_azalea shrub), `ironFence` along z=2: stone_bricks curb y0 + iron_bars y1 (+ `stone_brick_wall` posts every 3rd at y1), gaps x3..6 and x11..13; cheek wins at x10,x14. P6. Vocab: `ironFence`, `flowerBed`.
- [x] **14 Party walls close on both sides**: x=0 and x=15, z7..30, y0..18, `bricks`, blank (neighbours are implied by the blank brick). P1.
- [ ] **15 Deep back garden with deck**: deck posts (spruce_fence) at plan cells y3 (up to deck), deck `spruce_planks` top y4 x1..14 z31..35, joist `spruce_stairs`/`spruce_slab` fascia, railing `spruce_fence` y5 on z=35 (gap x6..8) and x1/x14 sides, step `spruce_stairs` at (6..8,3,36) facing south ascending north; lawn `grass_block` to y2, gravel path x7..8, retaining step `stone_brick_slab` y3 z44, upper garden y3. P6. Vocab: `deck`, `gardenBed`.
- [ ] **16 Tree**: trunk `oak_log` (12,3..7,41) (grade there y2, so trunk from y3), canopy `oak_leaves` persistent=true sphere r=3 centre (12,9,41) (y7..10 per plan). P6. Vocab: `tree`.
- [ ] **17 Raised vegetable beds, side flower beds, fences**: beds `farmland` with `spruce_slab`-free rim of `spruce_planks` (y3, soil y4 per plan), side borders `coarse_dirt` + flowers; board fences `spruce_fence` 2 high at x=0, x=15 (z31..49) and z=49. P6. Vocab: `gardenBed`.
- [ ] **18 Chimney**: `bricks` stack x0..2 z12..13 y18..19, cap `stone_brick_slab` at y20, two `brick_wall` flue pots on the cap at (1,21,12),(1,21,13). P3. Vocab: `chimney`.
- [ ] **19 Skylight**: opening x6..9 z15..17 y17 left by P3; glazed with `glass` by P4; curb of `smooth_quartz_slab` type=bottom at y18 around it. Vocab: `skylight`.
- [ ] **20 Rear façade**: BODY siding, stone base y0..3, windows per OPENINGS with flat cream hoods, French doors, 1-proud cornice y17 z=31, parapet y18 z=30. P1 (wall), P4 (glazing), P3 (cornice/parapet).
- [ ] **21 Rusticated stone plinth + water table**: `rusticated`, trim string y3 proud (z=3) and ledge slabs y4. P2.
- [ ] **22 Exterior lights**: `lantern` hanging=true at (12,8,8) in the porch ceiling; `lantern` standing on the cheek tops at (10,5,6) and (14,5,6). P5.
- [ ] **23 Interior (rooms)**: entry hall + long stair along E party wall (x13..14 z11..16), parlour behind bay with fireplace x=1 z11..13, dining, kitchen to garden, upstairs bedrooms front/back, bathroom clawfoot tub, top-floor room under the roof with skylight. Built by the rooms' designers; P1 builds the shells, partitions, slabs, stairs.
- [ ] **24 Stair runs**: garage→main (13..14, y=z-25, z26..29), main→2 (13..14, y=5+(z-12), z12..16), 2→3 (13..14, y=10+(z-19), z19..22), `*_stairs` facing south bottom; slab holes as per RESERVED. P1 builds the holes, the rooms' designers the stairs.
----
// Shared vocabulary for sfvictorian-split: the palette as named constants, the site coordinates from plan.md, and one
// helper per plan.md VOCABULARY item. Every helper writes through the build library (B.* states) into a Grid or a
// guard()/runParts() view, so a part can call the helpers it needs and nothing else.
//
// Conventions (plan.md): front is NORTH (z = 0 street, z grows south to the back fence). A stair's `facing` is the side
// of its full-height back. Cornice and bracket lips point at the street: half "top", facing "south" (into the wall).
import { B } from "/Volumes/ext1/swe/repos/minecraft-design/tools/src/build.mjs";

// ---- palette (ids from palette.json; B.* adds _stairs / _slab / _trapdoor / _door / _fence / _wall) ----------------
export const BODY = "cyan_terracotta";            // BODY siding (sage-teal)
export const TRIM = "smooth_quartz";              // TRIM cream: + stairs / slab
export const PILLAR = "quartz_pillar";            // corner boards, column shafts
export const PLUM = "crimson";                    // PLUM: + planks / stairs / slab / trapdoor / door / fence
export const PLUM_PANEL = "purple_terracotta";    // spandrel bands
export const GOLD = "yellow_terracotta";          // fish scale, pediment tympanum
export const GOLD_ALT = "orange_terracotta";      // fish scale second tone
export const STONE = "stone_bricks";              // BASE stone, full block
export const STONE_FAMILY = "stone_brick";        // BASE stone: + _stairs / _slab / _wall
export const ANDESITE = "andesite";               // rustication
export const CHISELED = "chiseled_stone_bricks";  // string course
export const BRICK = "bricks";                    // party walls, chimney, full block
export const BRICK_FAMILY = "brick";              // party walls: + _stairs / _slab / _wall
export const IRON = "iron_bars";                  // fences, handrails
export const PANE = "glass_pane";
export const GLASS = "glass";                     // skylight
export const CONCRETE = "light_gray_concrete";    // sidewalk, drive
export const GRAVEL = "gravel";                   // path, roof deck
export const DIRT = "dirt";                       // flower-bed soil
export const COARSE_DIRT = "coarse_dirt";         // side borders
export const FARMLAND = "farmland";               // raised vegetable beds
export const GRASS = "grass_block";               // lawn
export const TIMBER_PLANKS = "spruce_planks";     // deck, bed rims
export const TIMBER = "spruce";                   // + stairs / slab / fence / trapdoor
export const LOG = "oak_log";                     // tree trunk
export const LEAVES = "oak_leaves";               // canopy (persistent)
export const AZALEA = "flowering_azalea";         // flower-bed shrub
export const FLOWERS = ["red_tulip", "poppy", "allium", "azure_bluet", "lilac"];
export const LANTERN = "lantern";
export const END_ROD = "end_rod";                 // finials

// ---- site coordinates from plan.md (x 0..15 W->E, z 0 street/N -> 49 back fence, y 0 = street) ------------------
export const SITE = {
  lot: { x0: 0, x1: 15, z0: 0, z1: 49 },
  streetZ: 0,
  frontZ: 7,                  // main front wall
  rearZ: 30,                  // rear wall
  partyW: 0, partyE: 15,      // party walls
  parapetY: 18,
  deckY: 17,                  // roof deck (skylight, cornice course)
  cornice: { y: 17 },
  brackets: { y: 16 },
  pediment: { x0: 6, x1: 9, y: 19 },
  sidewalk: { x0: 0, x1: 15, z0: 0, z1: 1 },
  drive: { x0: 3, x1: 6, z0: 0, z1: 3 },
  plinth: { x0: 1, x1: 8, y0: 0, y1: 3, z0: 4, z1: 6, stringY: 3 },
  garageDoor: { x0: 3, x1: 6, y0: 1, y1: 3, z: 4 },
  bay: {
    y0: 4, y1: 16,
    rows: [{ z: 4, x0: 3, x1: 6 }, { z: 5, x0: 2, x1: 7 }, { z: 6, x0: 1, x1: 8 }],
    windowYs: [[5, 7], [10, 12], [14, 15]],   // S1, S2, S3 window heads (openings left air)
    faceWindowXs: [4, 5],                     // the face pair; the diagonals are single windows
    spandrelY: 9,
    fishScaleY: 13,
    cornerXs: [3, 6],
  },
  porch: { x0: 10, x1: 14, z0: 7, z1: 9, floorY: 4, voidY0: 5, voidY1: 8, ceilingY: 9, columnXs: [10, 14], columnZ: 7, wainscotXs: [9, 15], wainscotZs: [8, 9] },
  entry: { x0: 11, x1: 12, y: 5, z: 10, transomY: 8, casingXs: [10, 13] },
  stoop: { x0: 11, x1: 13, treads: [[1, 2], [2, 3], [3, 4], [4, 5]], landing: { y: 4, z: 6 }, cheekXs: [10, 14], cheekZ0: 2, cheekZ1: 6, cheekTops: [1, 2, 3, 4, 4] },
  ironFence: { z: 2, y: 1, segments: [[0, 2], [7, 10], [14, 15]] },   // gaps: drive 3..6, stoop 11..13
  flowerBeds: {
    westFront: { x0: 0, x1: 2, z0: 2, z1: 3 },
    eastFront: { x0: 7, x1: 10, z0: 2, z1: 3 },
    stoopSide: { x0: 14, x1: 15, z0: 2, z1: 6 },
    strip: { x0: 9, x1: 9, z0: 4, z1: 6 },
  },
  chimney: { x0: 0, x1: 2, z0: 12, z1: 13, y0: 18, y1: 19, capY: 20 },
  skylight: { x0: 6, x1: 9, z0: 15, z1: 17, y: 17 },
  deck: {
    x0: 1, x1: 14, z0: 31, z1: 35, y: 4,
    posts: [[1, 31], [14, 31], [1, 35], [7, 35], [14, 35]], postY: 3,
    railY: 5, railGap: [6, 8],
    steps: { x0: 6, x1: 8, y: 3, z: 36 },
  },
  tree: { x: 12, z: 41, trunkY0: 3, trunkY1: 7, canopyY0: 7, canopyY1: 10, canopyCenterY: 9, r: 3 },
  raisedBeds: [{ x0: 1, x1: 4, z0: 45, z1: 47 }, { x0: 11, x1: 14, z0: 45, z1: 47 }],
};

// ---- small utilities --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
const span = (a, b) => {
  const out = [];
  for (let i = Math.min(a, b); i <= Math.max(a, b); i++) out.push(i);
  return out;
};
const at = (g, x, y, z) => g.blockAt(x, y, z).replace("minecraft:", "");   // block id without namespace

// ---- VOCABULARY helpers -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/** siding(x,y,z): plain BODY cyan_terracotta. */
export function siding(g, x, y, z) {
  g.set(x, y, z, BODY);
}

/** rusticated(box): stone_bricks fill; odd y and odd x = andesite; the string course row (plinth stringY) = chiseled. */
export function rusticated(g, a, b) {
  for (const y of span(a[1], b[1])) for (const x of span(a[0], b[0])) for (const z of span(a[2], b[2])) {
    const block = y === SITE.plinth.stringY ? CHISELED : y % 2 === 1 && x % 2 === 1 ? ANDESITE : STONE;
    g.set(x, y, z, block);
  }
}

/** fishscale(x0,x1,y0,z): two rows at y0, y0+1. Row y0 gold with gold_alt on every 2nd x; row y0+1 is the offset. */
export function fishscale(g, x0, x1, y0, z) {
  for (const x of span(x0, x1)) {
    const alt = (x - x0) % 2 === 0;               // orange on the even cells of row y0
    g.set(x, y0, z, alt ? GOLD_ALT : GOLD);
    g.set(x, y0 + 1, z, alt ? GOLD : GOLD_ALT);   // offset by one: orange where row y0 is gold
  }
}

/** spandrel(x0,x1,y,z): PLUM_PANEL row at y, with a cream bottom-slab moulding proud at z-1. */
export function spandrel(g, x0, x1, y, z) {
  for (const x of span(x0, x1)) {
    g.set(x, y, z, PLUM_PANEL);
    g.set(x, y, z - 1, ...B.slab(TRIM, "bottom"));
  }
}

/** sill(x0..x1, y, z): cream top-slab sill (proud). */
export function sill(g, x0, x1, y, z) {
  for (const x of span(x0, x1)) g.set(x, y, z, ...B.slab(TRIM, "top"));
}

/** hoodPair(x0,x1,y,z): two crimson stairs meeting at a ridge (x0 faces east, x1 faces west), cream eaves at x0-1, x1+1. */
export function hoodPair(g, x0, x1, y, z) {
  g.set(x0, y, z, ...B.stairs(PLUM, "east", "bottom"));
  g.set(x1, y, z, ...B.stairs(PLUM, "west", "bottom"));
  g.set(x0 - 1, y, z, ...B.slab(TRIM, "bottom"));
  g.set(x1 + 1, y, z, ...B.slab(TRIM, "bottom"));
}

/** hoodSingle(x,y,z): one cream bottom-slab hood cell. */
export function hoodSingle(g, x, y, z) {
  g.set(x, y, z, ...B.slab(TRIM, "bottom"));
}

/**
 * window(x0,x1,y0,y1,z,face): glass_pane fill in the opening; for a front face ("north", the default) casing (cream,
 * proud at z-1, skipped where a casing or corner board already is), a sill at y0-1 and a hood at y1+1; hood is a pair
 * for 2+ wide openings and a single for 1 wide, unless opts.hood is "slab" (flat cream bottom-slabs across the head).
 * For a rear face ("south"): flat cream bottom-slab hood at y1+1, proud at z+1; no casing, no sill.
----
// Site build: the full lot grid, the grade, then every part in plan order (each part only adds; see runParts).
// Usage: node build.mjs <out.nbt>
import { Grid, runParts } from "/Volumes/ext1/swe/repos/minecraft-design/tools/src/build.mjs";
import * as shell from "./parts/shell.mjs";
import * as front from "./parts/front.mjs";
import * as roofs from "./parts/roofs.mjs";
import * as openings from "./parts/openings.mjs";
import * as ornament from "./parts/ornament.mjs";
import * as site from "./parts/site.mjs";
import * as room1 from "./parts/room-1.mjs";
import * as room2 from "./parts/room-2.mjs";
import * as room3 from "./parts/room-3.mjs";
import * as room4 from "./parts/room-4.mjs";
import * as room5 from "./parts/room-5.mjs";
import * as room6 from "./parts/room-6.mjs";
import * as room7 from "./parts/room-7.mjs";
import * as room8 from "./parts/room-8.mjs";
import * as room9 from "./parts/room-9.mjs";
import * as room10 from "./parts/room-10.mjs";
import * as room11 from "./parts/room-11.mjs";
import * as room12 from "./parts/room-12.mjs";
import * as room13 from "./parts/room-13.mjs";
import * as room14 from "./parts/room-14.mjs";
import * as room15 from "./parts/room-15.mjs";
import * as room16 from "./parts/room-16.mjs";
import * as room17 from "./parts/room-17.mjs";
import * as room18 from "./parts/room-18.mjs";

const out = process.argv[2];
if (!out) { console.error("usage: node build.mjs <out.nbt>"); process.exit(1); }

// x 0..15 street to party walls, y 0..21 (chimney pots at y21), z 0..49 lot line to back fence
const g = new Grid([16, 22, 50]);

// the grade: one grass layer over the lot; parts may replace it (it is set before runParts)
g.fill([0, 0, 0], [15, 0, 49], "minecraft:grass_block");

runParts(g, [
  ["shell and floors", shell.build],
  ["plinth, bay, porch, stoop", front.build],
  ["roof deck and rooflines", roofs.build],
  ["glazing and window dressing", openings.build],
  ["ornament", ornament.build],
  ["site and gardens", site.build],
  ["room: Garage", room1.build],
  ["room: Laundry and workshop", room2.build],
  ["room: Cellar store", room3.build],
  ["room: Cellar stair", room4.build],
  ["room: Entry hall", room5.build],
  ["room: Front parlour", room6.build],
  ["room: Parlour bay", room7.build],
  ["room: Dining room", room8.build],
  ["room: Kitchen", room9.build],
  ["room: Front bedroom", room10.build],
  ["room: Bedroom bay", room11.build],
  ["room: Study", room12.build],
  ["room: Upstairs landing", room13.build],
  ["room: Bathroom", room14.build],
  ["room: Back bedroom", room15.build],
  ["room: Top room", room16.build],
  ["room: Top bay", room17.build],
  ["room: Box room", room18.build],
], { palette: "palette.json" });

console.log(`# saved ${g.save(out)}`);

